## 2. Authentication & Registration Module

### 2.1 Login Page

**Route**: `GET /Login/Login` → `POST /Login/Login`

**Workflow**:
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["User opens Login page"] --> B["Enter Username + Password + CAPTCHA"]
    B --> C{"CAPTCHA valid?"}
    C -->|No| D["Show 'Error: captcha is not valid'"]
    C -->|Yes| E{"Username exists?"}
    E -->|No| F["Show 'Invalid Credentials'"]
    E -->|Yes| G["Decrypt stored password via AES"]
    G --> H{"Passwords match?"}
    H -->|No| F
    H -->|Yes| I["Set Session: UserID, Username"]
    I --> J{"Check assigned role"}
    J -->|SuperAdmin roleId=1| K["Redirect → SuperDashboard"]
    J -->|User roleId=2| L["Redirect → UserDashboard"]
    J -->|Admin roleId=3| M["Redirect → AdminDashboard"]
    J -->|No role assigned| N["Show 'Access Not Assigned'"]
```

**Input Fields**:

| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Username` | text | ✅ | `[Required]` "Username Required" | User's login identifier |
| `Password` | password | ✅ | `[Required]` "Password Required" | User's secret credential |
| `CAPTCHA` | image + text | ✅ | Server-side via `CaptchaMvc` | Bot prevention |

**Backend Interactions**:
- `IUserMaster.CheckUsernameExists(username)` — Check if login exists
- `IUserMaster.GetUserByUsername(username)` — Fetch user record
- `IPassword.GetPasswordbyUserId(userId)` — Fetch encrypted password
- `AesAlgorithm.DecryptString(encryptedPassword)` — Decrypt for comparison
- `ISavedAssignedRoles.GetAssignedRolesbyUserId(userId)` — Determine user's role
- Role IDs from `Web.config` AppSettings: `SuperAdminRolekey`, `UserRolekey`, `AdminRolekey`

### 2.2 Logout

**Route**: `GET /Login/Logout`

**Workflow**:
1. Clear HTTP cache headers (no-cache, no-store)
2. Expire "WebTime" cookie
3. Clear session → `Session.Clear()` + `Session.Abandon()`
4. Redirect to Login page

### 2.3 Registration Page (Self-Service)

**Route**: `GET/POST /Registration/Register`  
**Authorization**: `[AllowAnonymous]` — No login required

**Workflow**:
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["User opens Registration page"] --> B["Fill: Username, Name, Email, Mobile, Password"]
    B --> C{"Submit"}
    C --> D{"Username exists? — AJAX: CheckUsername"}
    D -->|Yes| E["Show 'Username already exists'"]
    D -->|No| F["Create Usermaster record"]
    F --> G["Encrypt password via AES"]
    G --> H["Save PasswordMaster record"]
    H --> I["Show 'Registration Successful'"]
```

**Input Fields**:

| Field | Type | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `UserName` | text | ✅ | Login username |
| `FirstName` | text | ✅ | First name |
| `LastName` | text | ✅ | Last name |
| `EmailId` | email | ✅ | Email address |
| `MobileNo` | text | ✅ | Mobile number |
| `Gender` | select | ✅ | Gender |
| `Password` | password | ✅ | Password (AES encrypted before storage) |
| `ConfirmPassword` | password | ✅ | Must match Password |

> [!NOTE]
> Registration does NOT assign a role. An admin must assign the role separately via the "Assign Role to User" page. Until a role is assigned, the user cannot access any dashboard.

**AJAX Endpoints**: `GET /Registration/CheckUsername?username=` — Real-time duplicate check

**Backend**: `IUserMaster.AddUser()`, `IPassword.SavePassword()`

